# AGENTS.md

Local ReAct + MCP agent project. Read `README.md` first and
`docs/architecture.md` before changing the loop or transports.

## Commands

Run through `uv`, not a bare `python` or `pytest`.

- Setup: `uv sync --all-extras`
- Lint: `uv run ruff check .`
- Format: `uv run ruff format src tests`
- Format check: `uv run ruff format --check src tests`
- Fast tests: `uv run pytest -q -m "not integration"`
- All tests: `uv run pytest -q`
- One test: `uv run pytest -q tests/test_react_agent.py::test_action_then_final`
- Chat: `uv run {{ cli_name }} repl`
- One-shot: `uv run {{ cli_name }} ask "..."`
{% if include_mcp_server %}
- MCP server: `uv run {{ cli_name }} serve`
{% endif %}
- Direct tool call: `uv run {{ cli_name }} call calculator --args '{"expression":"2+2"}'`

`{{ cli_name }} doctor` and `ask` need a reachable model. The test suite does
not: it uses `FakeLLM`.

## Architecture invariants

- The loop is **text ReAct**, not native tool calling. Preserve
  `stop=["Observation:"]`, the forgiving parser, and the `Final Answer:`
  contract or agent tests will break.
- `agent/react.py` depends only on the `LLM` protocol and `MCPToolClient`
  protocol. Do not import a provider or the MCP SDK there.
- `agent/parser.py` is deliberately forgiving. Add cases to
  `tests/test_parser.py` before changing it.
- `mcp_client/base.py` owns `ToolSpec`/`ToolResult`. The agent never sees raw
  MCP content blocks.
{% if include_mcp_server %}
- `server.py:create_server()` is the single registration point for tools.
  The module-level `mcp = create_server()` keeps `mcp dev` working.
- The stdio server command defaults to `sys.executable -m {{ package_name }}.server`
  in `MCPClient._stdio_params()`. Set `{{ env_prefix }}SERVER_COMMAND` to a JSON
  list to launch an external server instead.
{% else %}
- `MCPClient._stdio_params()` launches the command in
  `{{ env_prefix }}SERVER_COMMAND` (a JSON list). Set that variable, or use
  `{{ env_prefix }}TRANSPORT=http` with `{{ env_prefix }}SERVER_URL`.
{% endif %}
- `Settings.server_env()` decides what reaches the stdio child. Add every new
  server-side setting there; the child does not inherit `.env` automatically.
{% if include_mcp_server %}
- stdio is the default transport. `serve --http` binds `127.0.0.1` without
  auth; do not expose it publicly.
{% else %}
- stdio is the default transport.
{% endif %}

## Configuration

- `Settings` uses the `{{ env_prefix }}` prefix and loads `.env` from the working
  directory. CLI flags override environment values.
- Paths resolve against the current working directory. Run commands from the
  project root or use absolute paths.
- Traces live in `traces/`{% if include_sessions %}; sessions in `data/sessions/`{% endif %}.

{% if include_mcp_server %}
## Tools

Implement logic on `Toolbox` in `tools.py`, then register a thin wrapper in
`register_tools()`. Decorator order matters:

```python
@mcp.tool(title="...", annotations=ToolAnnotations(read_only_hint=True))
@instrumented
def my_tool(expression: str) -> str:
    return expression
```

`@instrumented` must be closest to the function. It uses `functools.wraps`, so
the SDK still sees the original signature and builds a clean JSON schema.

For progress, logs, or elicitation, make the tool `async` and add a
`ctx: Context` parameter. The SDK injects it and hides it from the schema. Wrap
blocking I/O with `asyncio.to_thread`.

{% endif %}
## Tests

- Use the `settings` fixture from `tests/conftest.py`; it isolates traces and
  sessions in `tmp_path`.
- `pytest-asyncio` runs in auto mode: plain `async def test_...` works.
- Mark tests that launch a real server subprocess with
  `@pytest.mark.integration`.
- Agent tests use `FakeLLM`/`FakeClient`; assert prompts, actions, and
  observations without a model.
- Do not add tests that hit a live model or network.

